instruction:
You are tasked with designing a module that implements a 4-input AND gate using only 3-input NAND gates. You should create a module with the following interface:

```
module JAND4B(A1, A2, A3, A4, O);
input   A1;
input   A2;
input   A3;
input   A4;
output  O;
// your code here
endmodule
```

Your module should implement the following logic: `O = A1 & A2 & A3 & A4`, where `&` denotes the logical AND operation. You should only use the provided `JNAND3B` module and instantiate it as necessary.

To complete this task, you should follow these steps:
1. Instantiate the `JNAND3B` module to create a 3-input NAND gate.
2. Use the 3-input NAND gate to create a 2-input NAND gate.
3. Use the 2-input NAND gate to create a 4-input NAND gate.
4. Use the 4-input NAND gate to implement the 4-input AND gate.

Your module should be able to pass the following test cases:

```
// Test case 1: All inputs are high
A1 = 1;
A2 = 1;
A3 = 1;
A4 = 1;
O = 1;

// Test case 2: One input is low
A1 = 1;
A2 = 0;
A3 = 1;
A4 = 1;
O = 0;

// Test case 3: Two inputs are low
A1 = 1;
A2 = 0;
A3 = 1;
A4 = 0;
O = 0;

// Test case 4: Three inputs are low
A1 = 1;
A2 = 0;
A3 = 0;
A4 = 0;
O = 0;

// Test case 5: All inputs are low
A1 = 0;
A2 = 0;
A3 = 0;
A4 = 0;
O = 0;
```

original_rtl:
module JAND4B(A1, A2, A3, A4, O);
input   A1;
input   A2;
input   A3;
input   A4;
output  O;

wire n1, n2, n3;

JNAND3B g1(n1, A1, A2, A3);
JNAND3B g2(n2, n1, A4, n1);
JNAND3B g3(n3, n2, n2, n2);
JNAND3B g4(O, n3, n3, n3);

endmodule

